#. help page 370: title
msgctxt "help/370/0"
msgid "Help with Wells"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/370/1"
msgid ""
"A well is a cheap way to create a water supply for a relatively small "
"area. Wells do not create any pipe access. They can be built anywhere, "
"but they only supply a primitive water supply that will limit land "
"values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#371Tips# "
msgstr ""

#. help page 371: title
msgctxt "help/371/0"
msgid "Tips for Wells"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/371/1"
msgid ""
"If you're the unsavory sort that builds \"slums\" to supply businesses "
"with convenient workers, you may find wells to be a cheap source of "
"water for them.  Housing near businesses can't grow into mansions "
"anyway, so a primitive water supply shouldn't be of much concern. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
