#. help page 385: title
msgctxt "help/385/0"
msgid "Fountains"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/385/1"
msgid ""
"Fountains create the largest area of water supply. A fountain must be "
"placed within a reservoir's zone of pipe access. It will then use the "
"pipe access to create a usable water supply for the area around it. "
"Multiple fountains can draw from a single reservoir. Building a network "
"of fountains supplied by reservoirs is a very effective way of "
"supplying your city with water.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#386Tips# / #387History#"
msgstr ""

#. help page 386: title
msgctxt "help/386/0"
msgid "Tips for Fountains"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/386/1"
msgid ""
"By building fountains at the farthest corners of a reservoir's area of "
"pipe access, you can cover a large square area with water supply.  "
"However, this doesn't mean that these are the most convenient locations "
"for fountains in your city. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#385Help# / #387History#"
msgstr ""

#. help page 387: title
msgctxt "help/387/0"
msgid "The Fountains of Rome"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/387/1"
msgid ""
"The Trevi Fountain\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#388Next Page#\n"
"#385Help#/#386Tips#"
