#. help page 475: title
msgctxt "help/475/0"
msgid "Help with Barracks"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/475/1"
msgid ""
"Barracks send soldiers out to patrol the city in search of Barbarians "
"and rioters. Soldiers will take the initiative to attack and kill any "
"such undesirables. They will also enhance the security level of any "
"areas they walk past (within a range of a few map squares). Ironically, "
"although Barracks protect and serve the city, residents hate to live "
"near them, and they limit land value. Residential areas should ideally "
"have good road access to barracks, but be at least several squares away "
"from them.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#476Tips# / #447 History#"
msgstr ""

#. help page 476: title
msgctxt "help/476/0"
msgid "Tips for Barracks"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/476/1"
msgid ""
"If you have built a wall around your city, you can better defend it by "
"building a road just inside the wall, and placing barracks next to that "
"road at regular intervals.  Make sure you build gates on the road as "
"well, so that your soldiers can reach enemies before they enter the "
"city. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#475Help# / #447 History#"
msgstr ""

