msgctxt "help/550/0"
msgid "Help with Circuses"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/550/1"
msgid ""
"The circus is an oblong track where chariot races are held. The larger "
"Circus Maximus is an impressive building that will draw huge crowds and "
"impact a larger region. Circuses are rectangular in shape.\n"
"\n"
"You may place one in any orientation in your city by using the rotate "
"arrows on your control panel.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#551Tips# / #552History#"
msgstr ""

#. help page 551: title
msgctxt "help/551/0"
msgid "Tips for Entertainment "
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/551/1"
msgid ""
"When you have access to improved entertainment, you should consider "
"\"upgrading\" the ones you have already built.  You can easily replace "
"your old ones with odeums and coliseums, as they take up the same "
"space.  On the other hand, the Circus Maximus is larger than the "
"Circus, so you plan to clear extra space for it.\n"
"\n"
"If you can't afford to build the more expensive forms of entertainment, "
"you should still prepare space for them in your city.  For example, if "
"you try to arrange as many city blocks around a clearing that will "
"eventually hold a circus, than you won't need to build so many "
"circuses. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#550Help# / #552History#"
msgstr ""

#. help page 552: title
msgctxt "help/552/0"
msgid "The Roman Circus"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/552/1"
msgid ""
"The prescription of the writer Juvenal for a happy citizenry came down "
"to two essentials: \"Bread and Circuses.\"  Juvenal undoubtedly selected "
"circuses because the chariot races held in these buildings were the "
"most popular spectator sport in the city of Rome.  Charioteers were "
"organized into teams by color -- the Greens, the Blues, the Reds, and "
"the Whites -- and their standings were hotly contested and wagered on. "
"Successful chariot drivers had fan clubs who followed their careers.\n"
"\n"
"At its height, Rome had a total of four circuses. The undisputed king "
"of these was the Circus Maximus, located in the valley between the "
"Palatine and \n"
"#553Next Page#\n"
"#550Help#/#551Tips#"
msgstr ""

#. help page 553: title
msgctxt "help/553/0"
msgid "The Roman Circus (Cont.)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/553/1"
msgid ""
"Aventine hills. It was essentially complete as early as 329 BC, "
"although it was modified and added onto as time went by.  This huge "
"structure measured 654 by 218 yards, roughly the size of a dozen or so "
"football fields laid side by side. It could seat somewhere between "
"255,000 and 385,000 racing enthusiasts at a time.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#552Previous Page#\n"
"#550Help#/#551Tips#"
msgstr ""

