#. help page 880: title
msgctxt "help/880/0"
msgid "Help with Forts"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/880/1"
msgid ""
"You may build as many as ten Cohort Forts in your Province, anywhere "
"except on mountains and atop other settlements. Each fort creates a "
"Cohort, or army, that you command. A Cohort will appear on your "
"Province Level map as an army beneath a waving battle standard, or "
"banner. The first Cohort you organize will be your Prima Cohors (First "
"Cohort), and each additional one will have its own name, makeup, and "
"ever-changing morale. The forces of your Legion (your entire armed "
"forces) will be divided evenly among the forts you build, so that the "
"more forts you have, the smaller each Cohort will be. You will manage "
"your Legion in your Forum.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#881Tips# / #882History#"
msgstr ""

#. help page 881: title
msgctxt "help/881/0"
msgid "Tips for Forts"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/881/1"
msgid ""
"At the start of the game, you may find it too expensive to build a "
"sizable legion.  Building too many forts will result in a very weak "
"cohorts.\n"
"\n"
"Once you have built provincial walls, make sure you have cohorts close "
"enough to them so that armies that attack the walls can be met before "
"they breach them.  The best way of doing this is to have different "
"cohorts on different areas of the map.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#880Help# / #882History#"
msgstr ""

#. help page 882: title
msgctxt "help/882/0"
msgid "Roman Forts"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/882/1"
msgid ""
"The Romans built hundreds, if not thousands, of temporary military "
"forts called casta during their conquest of the Mediterranean. There "
"was a standard design for each fort that the soldiers had to adhere to "
"during construction: a rectangular outer wall with a grid of streets "
"and a wide central area used as a forum, with each group of soldiers "
"having its own predetermined block of barracks.  The casta functioned "
"primarily as staging areas for the Empire's armies. Since their purpose "
"was usually offensive, not defensive, they were often sited at river "
"crossings and route intersections instead of defensible hilltops. A "
"number of these forts later grew into towns of the Middle Ages. \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#880Help#/#881Tips#"
msgstr ""

