#. help page 985: title
msgctxt "help/985/0"
msgid "Trading Posts"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/985/1"
msgid ""
"Trading Posts allow you to do business with lands outside your "
"Province. Goods will be sent to Trading Posts by border towns in your "
"Province. The closer a border town is to a Trading Post, the easier it "
"is for you to trade with that town. By building Trading Posts near "
"these towns on the edges of your Province Map, you will receive "
"valuable goods from each direction. You will also increase the demand "
"for exports in your city.\n"
"\n"
"To see which goods a border town will send to a Trading Post, go to the "
"Forum, and consult with the Merchant. Any Trading Post must have a "
"Warehouse adjacent to it, and must have road access to the capital "
"city. Trading Posts do not need Work Camps.\n"
"#986Tips#"
msgstr ""

#. help page 986: title
msgctxt "help/986/0"
msgid "Tips for Trading Posts"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/986/1"
msgid ""
"When choosing a location for a trading post, balance the advantage of "
"being close to a border town (increased trade) with the advantage of "
"being close to the city (it's less expensive to enclose within the "
"province's walls).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#985Help#"
msgstr ""

