#. help page 1112: title
msgctxt "help/1112/0"
msgid "Order Cohort"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/1112/1"
msgid ""
"This button allows you to select your Cohorts so that you may review "
"their status and give them orders.\n"
"\n"
"#1113Help with Cohorts#\n"
"#1114Tips for Cohorts#"
msgstr ""

#. help page 1113: title
msgctxt "help/1113/0"
msgid "Help with Cohorts"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/1113/1"
msgid ""
"By default, new recruits are sent equally into Cohorts, one assigned to "
"each Fort you have built on the Province Level. You may expand or "
"diminish a Cohort through the button on the Cohort info panel. The "
"\"Normal\" setting recruits an equal proportion of new troops (relative "
"to the other Cohorts), the \"Major\" setting sets a larger proportion, "
"and the \"Minor\" setting sets a smaller one. When a Cohort is set to "
"\"Demobilize,\" it will stop receiving new recruits from the training "
"pool, until you mobilize it again. \n"
"\n"
"The Order Cohort function allows you to issue orders to any of your "
"existing Cohorts.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1115Next Page#\n"
"#1114Tips#"
msgstr ""

#. help page 1114: title
msgctxt "help/1114/0"
msgid "Tips for Ordering Cohorts"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/1114/1"
msgid ""
"Set regular patrol routes to guard walls, your city, and any areas that "
"seem to regularly fall in the path of attacking armies.\n"
"\n"
"Remember that the longer you make a patrol route, the less likely it is "
"that a cohort will be in the \"right place at the right time.\"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1113Help#"
msgstr ""

#. help page 1115: title
msgctxt "help/1115/0"
msgid "Help with Cohorts (cont.)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/1115/1"
msgid ""
"You may set and assign patrol routes, send a Cohort after an enemy, or "
"to return the Cohort to its home fort. You may call upon your armies to "
"deal with several types of enemies.\n"
"\n"
"To issue orders, click on the Order Cohort button on the Province "
"Level. Your mouse pointer will change to a crosshair. Place it on the "
"Cohort you would like to command, and click.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#1113Previous Page# \n"
"#1114Tips#"
msgstr ""

#. help page 1116: title
msgctxt "help/1116/0"
msgid "Ports"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help/1116/1"
msgid ""
"Places ports to import and export goods via the sealanes to lands "
"outside your province. \n"
"\n"
"#1000Help with Ports#\n"
"#1001Tips for Ports#\n"
"#1002History of Ports#"
