#. help page 1150: title
msgctxt "help/1150/0"
msgid "All roads lead here..."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1151: title
msgctxt "help/1151/0"
msgid ""
"Thanks to our recent campaigns, the people of this province have been "
"\"Romanized.\"  They should be placid and welcoming."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1152: title
msgctxt "help/1152/0"
msgid ""
"This province is fairly quiet, but beware of occasional incursions of "
"the Gauls to the north."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1153: title
msgctxt "help/1153/0"
msgid ""
"There is a slight barbarian presence in this province, but it is a "
"prime trading area with access to the spice routes."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1154: title
msgctxt "help/1154/0"
msgid ""
"Your mission is to manage the small island of Sardinia, to the west of "
"Rome.  One of the outlying villages has not been tamed, so rule with "
"caution."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1155: title
msgctxt "help/1155/0"
msgid ""
"This province contains a village of those rebellious Gauls; however, "
"they should be fairly peaceable for their lot."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1156: title
msgctxt "help/1156/0"
msgid ""
"This region's once-great cities have been razed.  Rebuild this province "
"to even greater splendor, but beware a fierce and unruly populace."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1157: title
msgctxt "help/1157/0"
msgid ""
"This rich agricultural area is suitable for grapes and wheat, and its "
"ports should be a prime source of fish for the Empire."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1158: title
msgctxt "help/1158/0"
msgid ""
"This province allows enemies to reach the Empire from the south.  "
"Taming it would limit their incursions, but the people here seem "
"displeased with our presence."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1159: title
msgctxt "help/1159/0"
msgid ""
"Surveys report the soil here to be rich with ores and gems, and the "
"seas a prime source of fish."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1160: title
msgctxt "help/1160/0"
msgid ""
"The Gauls may have an important presence here, but they are more -- "
"civilized -- than most of their kind.  Resources are plentiful here."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1161: title
msgctxt "help/1161/0"
msgid ""
"As a southern province, this area would give us access to the ivory and "
"spice trading routes."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1162: title
msgctxt "help/1162/0"
msgid ""
"Mineral resources are not plentiful here, but the people recognize our "
"right to rule more than most of these barbarous lands."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1163: title
msgctxt "help/1163/0"
msgid ""
"The further north we expand, the fiercer the Gauls become.  However, "
"this region features some of the richest farmland the Empire has ever "
"seen."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1164: title
msgctxt "help/1164/0"
msgid ""
"This province is suited for cattle and wheat.  Beware the Greeks to the "
"south."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1165: title
msgctxt "help/1165/0"
msgid ""
"The Greeks' constant squabbling have made it easy for us to conquer "
"them.  However, that same contentious behavior will make them more "
"difficult for you to rule."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1166: title
msgctxt "help/1166/0"
msgid ""
"This island is small, yet rich in farmland and minerals.  However, the "
"populace may be troublesome."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1167: title
msgctxt "help/1167/0"
msgid ""
"There is a significant barbarian presence in these lands, but they seem "
"more passive than most.  The true threat must lie further north."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1168: title
msgctxt "help/1168/0"
msgid ""
"With the capacity for wheat farming in this province, this may be the "
"Empire's new breadbasket.  However, its inhabitants are less than "
"welcoming."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1169: title
msgctxt "help/1169/0"
msgid ""
"This region is rich in gems and other minerals, but among the mountains "
"lie many dangerous nomadic tribes."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1170: title
msgctxt "help/1170/0"
msgid ""
"Discontent is high in this area, which will make exploiting its "
"resources difficult."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1171: title
msgctxt "help/1171/0"
msgid ""
"This remote and rather rustic island offers some worthwhile exports, "
"but will have to remain well-defended to keep its rebellious populace "
"at bay."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1172: title
msgctxt "help/1172/0"
msgid ""
"Minerals are less prevalent here, and unrest will likely be a problem.  "
"Exercise caution when governing here."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1173: title
msgctxt "help/1173/0"
msgid ""
"This province is poised to become the most prosperous one in this "
"region, with plenty of farming and mineral resources."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1174: title
msgctxt "help/1174/0"
msgid ""
"This region looks promising, but the further east we expand, the more "
"powerful our enemies seem to become."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1175: title
msgctxt "help/1175/0"
msgid ""
"This province contains some villages that may cause trouble, but "
"overall it seems fairly quiet."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1176: title
msgctxt "help/1176/0"
msgid ""
"This province suffers from a lack of good farmland, and is threatened "
"by harassment from the north."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1177: title
msgctxt "help/1177/0"
msgid ""
"The people here are prone to rebellion, and have settled in many of the "
"outlying towns.  You must pacify the province, if you expect to keep "
"peace in your city."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1178: title
msgctxt "help/1178/0"
msgid ""
"This culture seems ripe for assimilation into our Empire, but the "
"threat of attack from the north looms over it."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1179: title
msgctxt "help/1179/0"
msgid ""
"The soil is quite fertile here, but the barbarian population is "
"significant.  Expect trouble."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1180: title
msgctxt "help/1180/0"
msgid ""
"The people here are strong, but seem willing to join the Empire.  "
"Beware invasions from the north."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1181: title
msgctxt "help/1181/0"
msgid ""
"This northern province contains a large barbarian presence, but its "
"resources seem worth the danger."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1182: title
msgctxt "help/1182/0"
msgid ""
"Farmland seems plentiful here, but the barbarians are also plentiful "
"and unwilling to join the Empire."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1183: title
msgctxt "help/1183/0"
msgid ""
"Resources are scarce on this small island, and the people look to be "
"difficult to manage.  Maintain vigilance."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1184: title
msgctxt "help/1184/0"
msgid ""
"Surveys show little in the way of resources, and resistance to the "
"Empire is strong here."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1185: title
msgctxt "help/1185/0"
msgid ""
"This region is a dangerous mix of excellent mineral resources and "
"rebellious villages.  Exploit the trade routes, and defend your capital "
"city."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1186: title
msgctxt "help/1186/0"
msgid ""
"This tiny empire may be good for little else but fish and frustration.  "
"Emperor, its inhabitants will bring you nothing but trouble."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1187: title
msgctxt "help/1187/0"
msgid ""
"Are you sure this a good idea?  Shouldn't we just wall off the northern "
"border of Britannia and be done with it?"
msgstr ""

#. help page 1188: title
msgctxt "help/1188/0"
msgid ""
"We've beaten back those upstart barbarians, and these lands are bereft "
"of minerals.  Perhaps it's best to leave sleeping dogs lie?"
msgstr ""

#. help page 1189: title
msgctxt "help/1189/0"
msgid ""
"Many barbarians have resettled in this area, thanks to our previous "
"campaigns.  Expanding into these lands would only give them a chance at "
"revenge -- in my humble opinion."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1190: title
msgctxt "help/1190/0"
msgid ""
"Aside from imported silks, is there anything to be gained from this "
"conquest but bloodshed?"
msgstr ""

#. help page 1191: title
msgctxt "help/1191/0"
msgid ""
"Our scouts in Dacia indicate that this area would be extremely "
"difficult to tame, though its silk trade and fishing waters are tempting."
msgstr ""

#. help page 1192: title
msgctxt "help/1192/0"
msgid ""
"Farming is difficult here, and our enemies are plentiful.  Are this "
"land's meager benefits worth provoking them further?"
msgstr ""

#. help page 1193: title
msgctxt "help/1193/0"
msgid ""
"This land is barren, and the Huns who travel across it are nearly a "
"match for our own troops!  I beg you to reconsider!"
msgstr ""

#. help page 1194: title
msgctxt "help/1194/0"
msgid "AVE  IMPERATOR!"
msgstr ""

